/target
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED. This crate is a binary -- a driver someone
# installs -- not a library, so the lockfile is the record of what a
# release was actually built from. Ignoring it meant `--locked` had
# nothing to check against and a dependency could move under a release
# without anything saying so.
*.img
.history
.test-env
test-diagnostics/
.claude/